      "benefit": "IP",
      "years": [2020, 2024],
      "pattern": "drift",
      "direction": "decrease",
      "magnitude": "~ -0.11 A/E points per year, falling from 1.16 to 0.67",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "evidence": [
        "ae_ip_by_year.csv: monotonic year-over-year decline from 1.158 (2020) to 0.667 (2024)",
        "Expected claims exceed 1,500/yr (Poisson SD < 0.03); 2024 value is >10 sigma below the 1.0 baseline",
        "ae_ip_termination.csv shows termination A/E ~1.0 across all diagnoses, ruling out faster recovery/termination rates as the driver"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate structural drivers of the falling IP A/E: analyze new claim incidence, average claim duration, and benefit amounts by year. Review pricing and reserving assumptions for IP incidence and duration. Check for product redesign, eligibility tightening, return-to-work initiatives, or economic factors affecting claim reporting."
    }
  ]
}

